package chain

// The compiled identity of AttestationRegistryV2, pinned in Go.
//
// Startup validation must not read the Hardhat artifact from disk: in a
// container it is not there, and if it were, an attacker able to write it could
// choose what the operator considers the expected contract. These values are
// therefore part of the binary, and TestRuntimeTemplateMatchesBuildInfo
// regenerates them from Hardhat's build-info so they cannot drift.

// ImmutableRef locates a Solidity `immutable` inside the runtime bytecode.
//
// The compiler emits an immutable at EVERY site that reads it, so there is more
// than one occurrence even for a single variable -- two here. Handling only the
// first would leave part of the code unverified.
type ImmutableRef struct {
	Start  int
	Length int
}

// RegistryV2PublisherImmutables are the offsets at which the `publisher`
// address is embedded in the runtime code, in ascending order.
var RegistryV2PublisherImmutables = []ImmutableRef{
	{Start: 122, Length: 32},
	{Start: 468, Length: 32},
}

// RegistryV2SolcVersion identifies the compiler that produced the template.
// A different compiler produces different bytecode for the same source, so a
// mismatch here is a real difference, not a formality.
const RegistryV2SolcVersion = "0.8.24+commit.e11b9ed9"

// RegistryV2DeployedTemplate is the runtime bytecode with the publisher
// immutable left as zeroes. Validation splices the deployed contract's actual
// publisher into these offsets and compares the WHOLE result, so both the code
// and the specific immutable are proven -- rather than masking the offsets out,
// which would leave the most security-relevant 40 bytes unchecked.
const RegistryV2DeployedTemplate = ""
